# seed: 6
# requires: hero_ready map_enter battle_start battle_flee_failed battle_fled
# requires-match: battle_flee_failed sticky=0 held=
# requires-match: battle_fled sticky=0
# FUN_00436c9d: fleeing. Offline, DAT_00502b14 is 0 for an ordinary encounter and the Tactics
# abandon dialog (FUN_00447431) returns 0, so the hero is NEVER given a timer escape: pressing F
# while nothing is animating on the hero is refused outright with "You attempt to flee... but are
# dragged back".
#
# The only way out is the original's 30 % interrupt, and that window is far narrower than it
# looks. FUN_00436c9d returns "blocked" on its first test whenever the hero's own record is 0x2F,
# and it SETS that record to 0x2F as a side effect, so the hero gets exactly one live roll per
# round and every later F in the same round is refused before the roll is ever reached. The roll
# itself (`fight.victim == 0 && state == ROUND_DAMAGE && !past(anim_start, duration_ms)`) is only
# open while a MONSTER's attack is animating on the hero. The hero therefore never presses A,
# and F is pressed exactly once per round, on the frame `battle_monster_act` reports the
# monster committing - the same frame FUN_0048f56c calls FUN_00490723, which stamps anim_start
# and enters ROUND_DAMAGE. Miss the frame and the round is burnt; the seed is pinned so the
# pinned round's 30 % draw is the one that lands.
#
# FUN_0041B891's own table (all.c:21078) has THREE states before the Well, not two:
#   1 main menu -> 2 "Where Do You Want To Play Today?" (splash, FUN_0041D31F)
#   2 -> 3 "Choose Your World" + the world list (FUN_0041D717)
#   3 -> take the highlighted row (msg 0x474) -> the Pick-a-Soul window
# RETURN is the plan's keyboard shortcut for the click.
#
# The Gateway of Dreams (map 0 link 0, SCENE 3) sits one cell south of the Evergreen
# spawn, and quest.txt:1774 makes its first visit an `ASK 30` -- the golden rule,
# "Do you agree to obey the golden rule? (type YES or NO)". An ASK suspends the scene
# until the player answers, so every script that walks into the link has to answer it
# the way a player does: Y (scene.c's ST_ASK sets the reply to "YES"). Left unanswered
# the scene waits forever and nothing downstream can fire. The Soul Brother also hands
# over L1 / H5000 / M5000 and a Ticket Home, opens the `OFFER2 0,10` shop, and sizes the
# trophy bag to 4x3, so this is a real visit and not a scripted cut to the fight.
expect boot_menu 900
# FUN_00402A73's Terms of Service modal opens on entry to the main menu (front.c:534
# tos_gate, consumed at front.c:770) and swallows the next key. "I Accept" is
# tos_accept = (356,371,75,23), so its centre is (393,382).
click 393 382
expect tos_accept 300
# State 2 is where FUN_0041F699 makes its synchronous 0x46F call, which raises
# SRNet's modal (0x42AA10). 1005 "Solo Game" is (250,313,299,23) -> centre
# (399,324); control 1 "Play Game" is (250,380,75,23) -> centre (287,391).
# 1005 then 1 closes it, 0x46F returns 1, FUN_0041D374 registers
# "--- Scanning ---", and the stepper FUN_00438E8E runs ~30 calls (6140 to
# 8340 ms) before FUN_0041B891(3) draws the world list.
# Main menu: RETURN is the Play-now shortcut (0x46B) into state 2.
key RETURN
wait 30
click 399 324
wait 10
click 630 309
wait 240
# State 3 is the world list; RETURN takes the highlighted row
# (msg 0x474), which is the keyboard shortcut for the row's click.
key RETURN
wait 30
key n
wait 5
text Tester
key RETURN
expect hero_ready 300
expect map_enter 600
keydown DOWN
expect scene_enter 600
keyup DOWN
wait 40
key RETURN
wait 40
key RETURN
wait 40
key RETURN
wait 40
key y
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 40
key RETURN
wait 40
expect panel_open 600
key ESCAPE
wait 20
